  "details": "I propose adding separate settings for the Avatar Download Size Limit: one for Friends and one for Non-Friends.\n\nThe current situation: Currently, the download size limit is applied universally. This forces users to choose between either blocking many of their friends' (potentially large) avatars, or allowing all non-friend avatars, which can lead to performance issues and security risks.\n\nThe main reason for this request is security: In Public worlds, there is a serious concern about malicious users utilizing crash or harmful avatars to intentionally degrade performance or crash other users' clients.\n\nThe proposed solution: By splitting the setting, users can set a very strict, low limit (e.g., 10-50MB) for Non-Friends to mitigate the risk of crashers, while setting a more lenient limit (e.g., 200MB+) for Friends to still enjoy their creative avatars. This offers a major improvement in performance management and security without compromising social interaction with friends.",
